BackgroundLong‐term drug treatment of schizophrenia with typical antipsychotic drugs has limitations: 25 to 33% of 
sufferers have illnesses that are treatment resistant. Clozapine is an antipsychotic drug, which is claimed to have 
superior efficacy and to cause fewer motor adverse effects than typical drugs for people with treatment‐resistant 
illnesses. Clozapine carries a significant risk of serious blood disorders, which necessitates mandatory weekly blood 
monitoring at least during the first months of treatment.ObjectivesTo evaluate the effects of clozapine compared with 
typical antipsychotic drugs in people with schizophrenia.cochranelibrary.com

